  "behavior": [
    "Pinned Unix OSD::SecSleep calls usleep with the native integer product and ignores its result.",
    "A signal directed to the sleeping thread interrupts the native call and returns early.",
    "The Rust NativeSleeper now uses usleep on Unix; injected Sleeper implementations keep their existing Duration callback.",
    "The Windows Sleep implementation was cross-compiled but not runtime tested."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only the positive 30-second input is the defined regression; signed integer overflow inputs are not claimed.",
    "The negative -1 native sample is exploratory pinned-glibc evidence for a useconds_t value outside the POSIX range.",
    "Osd::sec_sleep_with(custom_sleeper, ...) remains a Rust injection surface and does not model signals unless that sleeper chooses to."
  ]
